      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Frederick Stevens platted the area that would become East Port Orchard in 1886, naming it after his father, Sidney.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_Orchard%2C_Washington",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Nestled on Sinclair Inlet, East Port Orchard’s daily rhythm is set by tides and the ever‑present silhouette of the Olympic Mountains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wikixm.com/us/wa/east-port-orchard/overview",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "William Renton and Daniel Howard built the first sawmill in the area in 1854, sparking early settlement.",
